# Run E (2026-11-06): run D's setup (IQL, online freeze 1000, encoder + GRU
# frozen; il_finetune_c0_iql.env) plus three changes.
#
#  1. ACTOR_LOG_STD=-2.0: the actor's noise is pinned at the clone's own level
#     (log-std about -2.0 on replay states while run D's actor was still
#     frozen), so only the mean action trains. Every clone fine-tune collapsed
#     with its noise growing on the same states: SAC run C to the +2 cap, the
#     trunk-frozen SAC run to about -1.2, IQL run D from -2.0 to -0.8 (AWR fits
#     the noise to the EXECUTED actions: the recording's DART noise plus the
#     policy's own, which then feeds back through the replay).
#  2. IL_PRELOAD_ROOT adds the coverage recording, il_data_cover (480 episodes,
#     36.7k steps; user 2026-11-06 "PERTURB EXPERT MORE SO WE HAVE COVERAGE
#     DATA"): executed actions into the replay, clean labels into the cloning
#     buffer, as for il_data.
#  3. CRITIC_LAYERNORM=1 (user rule 2026-11-06; the trainer's default, set
#     here so the overlay says it). c0's critics have no LayerNorm, so they
#     start fresh; the clone never trained them.
#
# User 2026-11-06: stop run D; the next fine-tune was left to me ("No
# preference" between IQL, SAC or both, each pinned): IQL, as recommended.
. "$REPO/slurm/il_finetune_c0_iql.env"
export ACTOR_LOG_STD=-2.0 CRITIC_LAYERNORM=1
export IL_PRELOAD_ROOT=$HOME/carla-rl/checkpoints/il_data:$HOME/carla-rl/checkpoints/il_data_cover
